<urn:atm:triage:finding/AN15R-COMPOSITION-ERROR-CONFIG-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AN15R-COMPOSITION-ERROR-CONFIG-002" ;
  triage:title "composition_error() (compose_file() path) still collapses ComposeError::Config into the generic TemplateRenderVerificationFailed code, reproducing the AN15R-AMBIGUOUS-INSPECTION-ERROR-CODE-001 ambiguity on a sibling entrypoint" ;
  triage:description "PR #884 (fix/an15-templatehash-error-code-ambiguity, commit 28668949b19b0f9a368680f4661292298cf5362d) fixed AN15R-AMBIGUOUS-INSPECTION-ERROR-CODE-001 by splitting inspection_error() (crates/atm-template-sc-compose/src/lib.rs:97-105, used by inspect()) into a typed match that routes ComposeError::Config to the new AtmErrorCode::TemplateInspectionParseFailed via inspection_parse_error(). However composition_error() (lib.rs:78-87), the sibling helper used by compose_file() (the production method backing the local `atm compose` preview command, sole caller crates/atm/src/commands/compose.rs:66-69, production call site lib.rs:323 via sc_composer::compose()), was not updated: it still maps ComposeError::Validation | Render | Config uniformly to AtmErrorCode::TemplateRenderVerificationFailed. The same upstream ComposeError::Config condition (a frontmatter/config parse failure) therefore produces a different, code-inconsistent ATM error code depending on which of the adapter's two entrypoints handled it -- the same class of ambiguity the AN15R-AMBIGUOUS-INSPECTION-ERROR-CODE-001 fix was chartered to eliminate, just on compose_file() instead of inspect(). Independently confirmed by three sources: req-qa (ATM-QA-001, Important, FAIL), ruthless-boundary-qa (RBQA-F002-AN15R, Important), and rust-best-practices-agent (RBP-F001, Important), plus direct read of lib.rs:78-113 by quality-mgr. Does not resurrect the original TEMPLATE_HASH_API_FAILED code (composition_error never produced that code), so it is not a reopening of AN15R-AMBIGUOUS-INSPECTION-ERROR-CODE-001's original occurrence -- it is a new, narrower finding blocking that finding's full closure." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-an" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "diagnostics" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-15T00:50:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AN.15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-15T00:50:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AN15R-COMPOSITION-ERROR-CONFIG-002/AN15-OCC-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

